 "ref": "The money came through relationships. In his plea agreement, Horwitz admitted raising money from at least five major groups of private investors. He also admitted he understood that those groups raised part of their money from sub-investors who had no direct contract with one-in-M-M. The agreement put the number of those sub-investors at more than two hundred fifty, a figure he reserved the right to contest. Prosecutors said many of the investors were his personal friends. In other words, some of the money came from people who had no direct contract with one-in-M-M. Before you invest, know exactly who is on the other side of your contract.",
